{
  "$comment": "Each product's images in the Awebound Fourthwall shop, in the shop's order: the site shows them in the same order, the first as the listing image. `gallery`: `photo` entries are finished photos with their own background, cropped to the site's 4:5 frame (each piece's surface in compose.py is matched to its photos' background, and compose.py reports any photo that drifts from it); `render` entries are Fourthwall's cut-out renders, placed on the piece's own surface. `view` says what each shows. `frame` (on a photo framed tighter than the rest): the garment's height and top as fractions of the 4:5 frame, matching the other tees' full views; compose.py zooms the photo out to them with widen.py. An entry holds a file name under `photos` or `renders`, or a full address. `cutouts`: Fourthwall renders of the current print, by view, kept even when the shop no longer lists them; compose.py cuts the garment for the home page and the close-up from them. A view missing here (a print that changed since its render) falls back to `cutouts/<slug>-<view>.webp` in this folder. `holds` (when needed): Fourthwall images left out on purpose, and why. fourthwall.py downloads the gallery into fourthwall/ and the cutouts into fourthwall/renders/, and compose.py builds apps/web/public/products/<slug>/. When a product's images change in Fourthwall, run `fourthwall.py --sync <piece>` (public products only; for hidden ones, edit the list here from the shop's image list), check the views, then `fourthwall.py <piece>` and `compose.py <piece>`.",
